---
/* Component — PageHeaderCenter
 * The centre region of the page's top bar.
 *
 * Claims grid column 2 of PageHeader's `1fr auto 1fr` track list explicitly
 * rather than relying on source order. Because the two outer columns are equal
 * fractions, column 2 sits at the bar's centre regardless of whether either
 * sibling region is present — so a header carrying only a centre is genuinely
 * centred.
 *
 * justify-content: center centres the region's own content within the column,
 * which matters only when something else stretches the column. */
---

<div>
  <slot />
</div>

<style>
  div {
    grid-column: 2;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: var(--bravoixr-spacing-3);
  }
</style>
